## Summary

This is the `spring-petclinic-rest` Spring Boot app. Owner creation lives in the V1 REST controller, which delegates persistence to `ClinicServiceImpl.saveOwner(...)` and then emits an audit line via a dedicated `OwnerAuditLogger` writing to an SLF4J logger literally named `"AUDIT"`.

Note up front: there is currently **no `memberId` field** anywhere in the code. The only reference is in a test comment (`AcceptanceTest.java` line 10) describing a future switch of the audit event's identifier from `customerCode` to `memberId`. Today the audit uses `customerCode` as the primary identifier.

---

## 1. Owner creation

The creation entry point is `addOwner(...)` in the V1 controller (V2 only has a paged list endpoint, no create).

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java` (lines 158-206):

