The persistence + field-derivation happens in `saveOwner` at `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/service/ClinicServiceImpl.java` (lines 242-265). This is where `customerCode` and `membershipNumber` are generated:

```java
@Override
@Transactional
public void saveOwner(Owner owner) throws DataAccessException {
    if (owner.isNew() && owner.getCustomerCode() == null) {
        String region = LocalityResolver.regionFor(owner.getPostcode(), owner.getCity());
        String customerCode =
            customerCodeGenerator.generate(region, owner.getTelephone(), owner.getLastName());
        owner.setCustomerCode(deduplicateCustomerCode(customerCode));
    }
    if (owner.isNew() && owner.getNamesakeCount() == null) {
        owner.setNamesakeCount(countNamesakes(owner.getFirstName(), owner.getLastName()));
    }
    if (owner.isNew() && owner.getMembershipNumber() == null) {
        owner.setMembershipNumber(
            membershipNumberGenerator.generate(owner.getCustomerCode(), owner.getRegistrationDate()));
    }
    if (owner.isNew() && owner.getHouseholdSize() == null) {
        owner.setHouseholdSize(countHouseholdMembers(owner));
    }
    if (owner.isNew() && owner.getMembershipLevelCap() == null) {
        owner.setMembershipLevelCap(computeMembershipLevelCap(owner));
    }
    ownerRepository.save(owner);
}
```

Interface declaration: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/service/ClinicService.java` line 60.

---

## 2 & 5. Audit line and the AUDIT logger

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/OwnerAuditLogger.java` (full class). The logger is defined as a static SLF4J `Logger` named `"AUDIT"` (line 33), and a single audit line is emitted at INFO level:

```java
@Component
public class OwnerAuditLogger {

    private static final Logger AUDIT = LoggerFactory.getLogger("AUDIT");

    public void logCreated(Owner owner) {
        AUDIT.info("Owner created: id={} customerCode={} registrationDate={} membershipLevel={} membershipNumber={}",
            owner.getId(), owner.getCustomerCode(), owner.getRegistrationDate(),
            owner.getMembershipLevel(), owner.getMembershipNumber());
    }
}
```

Current format (after SLF4J placeholder substitution):
```
Owner created: id=<id> customerCode=<code> registrationDate=<date> membershipLevel=<level> membershipNumber=<number>
```

This is the only place an audit line is emitted. There is no `AuditService` class; the only audit component is `OwnerAuditLogger`. It is the sole caller of `logCreated` (from `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`, line 201).

There is currently **no structured/JSON audit event** — no `seq`, no `OWNER_CREATED` marker, no `event` field in production code (grep for `OWNER_CREATED`/`seq`/`event` in `src/main` returns nothing relevant). Those tokens only exist in the test/spec described below.

---

## 3. customerCode / membershipLevel / memberId on the Owner entity

Owner entity: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java` (extends `Person`).

Relevant fields/accessors:
- `customerCode` — persisted column `customer_code`, field at line 70-71, getter/setter lines 205-211. Its region prefix is also used by `getLocality()` (lines 493-500), `getCheckDigit()` (516-519).
- `membershipNumber` — column `membership_number`, field line 79-80, getter/setter 229-235.
- `membershipLevel` — **derived/`@Transient`**, not a column. `getMembershipLevel()` at lines 413-420, computed from `getMembershipPoints()` (391-406) and capped by `membershipLevelCap` (column `membership_level_cap`, lines 94-95).
- `memberId` — **does not exist** on the entity (or anywhere in `src/main`).

Other creation-captured fields on the entity: `registrationDate`, `householdId`, `namesakeCount`, `bulkSignupWarning`, `householdSize`, `postcode`, `possibleDuplicateOf`, `membershipLevelCap`, `deleted`.

(The class is 614 lines; the load-bearing snippets are the `customerCode` field/accessor at 70/205-211, `membershipNumber` at 79/229-235, and the transient `getMembershipLevel()` at 413-420 shown here.)

```java
